//!
//! # What `__Host-` means, and why one constructor owns it
//!
//! `__Host-` is not a naming convention. A user agent accepts a cookie whose
//! name carries the prefix only when the cookie sets `Secure`, sets `Path=/`,
//! and carries no `Domain` attribute. The three conditions must hold
//! together, and a cookie that fails any of them is **dropped silently**
//! rather than rejected loudly, so the failure surfaces later as an absent
//! session and never as an error at the point of the mistake.
//!
//! | Rule | Where it is enforced here |
